The meta.json file allows you to set authors, title, ratings, warnings, links, and credits.
Schema is at https://benheroblaw.github.io/meta_schema.json

NOBR>If you add "author": "your_name", it will display in the author section.
If you instead write "authors" it will display 'Authors: {meta_authors}' rather than 'Author: {meta_author}'.

NOBR>Add "rating": "your_rating" to set a rating.
NOBR>Ratings are 0-3.
0 = General Audiences, 1 = Teen, 2 = Explicit, 3 = Adult

Add "links": "your_links" to set links to your pages.

Add "warnings": "your_warnings" to set warnings.

Add "credits": "your_credits" to set credits.

Add "title": "your_title" to set the title.

CLRB>A fully-filled-out meta.json would look like this:
CONT>{
CONT>  "author": "benheroblaw",
CONT>  "title": "testing stuff",
CONT>  "rating": 1,
CONT>  "links": "https://benheroblaw.github.io",
CONT>  "warnings": "swearing",
CONT>  "credits": "benheroblaw for coding the whole thing"
}

And display as this:
CONT>Title:    testing stuff
CONT>Folder:   ./content/zzz-testing/
CONT>Rating:   Teen
CONT>Warnings: swearing
CONT>Author:   benheroblaw
CONT>Links:    https://benheroblaw.github.io
CONT>Credits:  benheroblaw for coding the whole thing